   Jim Frederick; section 5 and data/upstream/LICENSE carry that attribution.

   The bundled OIF PDFs remain the property of the Optical Internetworking
   Forum (section 2). data/spec_pdf_index.json and the derived SQLite rows
   contain ONLY factual identifiers: table numbers, short table captions,
   PDF page numbers, field names, byte addresses and access/requirement
   tokens. Verbatim specification prose - in particular field descriptions -
   is used transiently in memory for unit derivation and is NOT persisted.
   Short table captions are included as navigation identifiers, not as a
   reproduction of specification text.

   The coordinate-based extraction is best-effort. The published CSV and the
   OIF specification remain authoritative; verification numbers are a
   diagnostic aid, not a compliance statement. Provenance data is read-only
   and is never used for hardware writes.

   Two derived reports reuse the same reader without persisting any
   additional OIF prose:
     - tools/diff_spec_versions.py -> data/spec_version_diff.json and
       docs/CMIS_53_54_DIFF.md (5.3 vs 5.4 caption-level diff, item P-02)
     - tools/verify_seed_fields.py -> data/seed_field_verification.json and
       docs/SEED_FIELD_VERIFICATION.md (demo field cross-check, item P-01)
   Both contain ONLY factual identifiers (table numbers, short captions,
   page numbers, field names, byte addresses, access tokens and computed
   similarity/confidence grades). They are advisory review aids, never
   compliance statements. verify_seed_fields.py is strictly read-only and
   never modifies data/seed.json or the hardware write path.
